---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi3_46",
  "series": "Band VI 3 (1672-1676); durchgesehener Nachdruck 1980",
  "seq": 46,
  "text": "[[421.16]] <b>46. Schediasma de arte inveniendi theoremata </b> <span>421.16;0:63:046:74!      :L:l^</span>.\n[[421.17]] 7. September 1674\n[[422.1]] De Arte inveniendi Theoremata.\n[[422.2]] Artem problemata solvendi tantum ab Analyticis tractatam constat. Theoremata\n[[422.3]] autem fassi sunt omnes, casu inveniri: nam quis mortalium praevidere possit exitum\n[[422.4]] combinationum valde compositarum; constat autem ab eventu quodam inexpectato\n[[422.5]] combinationes quasdam consequente, theorematum elegantiam oriri. Quare combinationes\n[[422.6]] omnes ordine instituere necesse fuerit, elegantes eventus extundere volenti,\n[[422.7]] quod non est in humana potestate. Superest sane nonnihil in Artis combinatoriae\n[[422.8]] arcanis, quod huic negotio lucem affundere possit, sed hoc a nemine non dicam\n[[422.9]] erutum, sed ne suspicione quidem libatum est. Mihi vero in mentem venit ratio, qua\n[[422.10]] hoc saltem efficere possim, ut si quis proposito quodam argumento, theorema elegans\n[[422.11]] a me postulet, exhibendum intra certum tempus ausim dicere me satisfacturum. Tota\n[[422.12]] eius rei ratio huc redit:\n[[422.13]] Quaere solutionem Problematis cuiusdam, valde difficilis aut etiam impossibilis:\n[[422.14]] methodo quadam plausibili, id est in multis aliis casibus succedente; incides in progressu\n[[422.15]] in miras quasdam atque inexpectatas, eorum quibus uti volebas compensationes\n[[422.16]] sive destructiones, atque ita quanquam problema non solveris, theorema\n[[422.17]] tamen memorabile detexisti. Ita video inquisitionem Motus perpetui praeclara de\n[[422.18]] Aequilibrio theoremata protulisse.\n[[422.19]] Ego quoque dudum observaram proprietatem praeclaram, Ictus descendentium.\n[[422.20]] Nimirum ponamus Ictum corporis descendentis in subjectam lancem C, eoque motu\n[[422.21]] catenam ex globis continuatis compositam ita elevantis, ut D paulum\n[[422.22]] elevato ipsi A succedens etiam cadat, A autem ubi in locum B pervenerit\n[[422.23]] in locum E subintret. Unde sequitur ictum corporis ponderi totius\n[[422.24]] catenae aequivalere, alioquin si excederet, sequeretur motus perpetuus.\n[[422.25]] Hoc non demonstrationem sane dat, satis validam, sed inquirendi occasionem\n[[422.26]] praebet, nam postea demonstratio facilis, theoremate semel\n[[422.27]] oblato: eadem opera facile (theoremata) praeclara deteguntur in Geometria\n[[422.28]] aut Analysi, cuius exemplum apponam, dum reducere tento aequationes locorum\n[[422.29]] omnes ad duas aequationes ad circulum.\n[[423.1]] Esto aequatio ad Circulum:\n[[423.2]] ((Formel^y\n[[423.3]] \n[[423.4]] Et alia ad Conicam quamcunque\n[[423.5]] ((Formel^y\n[[423.6]] \n[[423.7]] Auferendo Unam ab altera, fiet Aequatio ad Parabolam\n[[423.8]] ((Formel^y\n[[423.9]] Sive\n[[423.10]] ((Formel^y\n[[423.11]] \n[[423.12]] \n[[423.13]] Aequatio ad Conicam mutetur in sequentem:\n[[423.14]] ((Formel^y\n[[423.15]] \n[[423.16]] Unde rursus auferendo Circularem, fiet alia ad Parabolam\n[[423.17]] ((Formel^y\n[[423.18]] Sive\n[[423.19]] ((Formel^y\n[[423.20]] \n[[423.21]] \n[[423.22]] Jungantur duae aequationes ad Parabolam 4 et 7, fiet Aequatio ad Circulum\n[[424.1]] ((Formel^y\n[[424.2]] Jam\n[[424.3]] ((Formel^y\n[[424.4]] Cumque idem sit in caeteris, hinc facile demonstratur: aequationem 8. nihil\n[[424.5]] differre ab aequatione 1.\n[[424.6]] Eademque opera invenimus Theorema elegans, quod analytice ita enuntiari potest:\n[[424.8]] ((Formel^y\n[[424.9]] quantitates autem o, n, m / l pro arbitrio sumi possunt.\n[[424.10]] Inventis semel (Theorematibus) facile est eorum combinatione alia multa invenire.\n[[424.11]] Exempli causa: duo habemus theoremata:\n[[424.12]] ((Formel^y\n[[425.2]] Et aliud:\n[[425.3]] ((Formel^y\n[[425.4]] Jungantur invicem per additionem: Summa fiet 2. Jungantur per subtractionem,\n[[425.5]] summa erit 0. Jungantur per multiplicationem vel divisionem, summa erit 1. Ac\n[[425.6]] totidem habebuntur theoremata sane mira, quorum si demonstrationem exhibeas\n[[425.7]] non indicato fonte, obstupefacies aliquando lectorem.\n[[425.8]] Alia ratio est investigandi Theoremata. Scis proprietatem quandam, vel solutionem\n[[425.9]] elegantem, sive ab alio demonstratam, sive casu et inductione inventam, investiga\n[[425.10]] calculo analytico, vel Geometrico ratiocinio, necessario tibi exhibebitur tandem\n[[425.11]] elegans theorema, quod te ex calculi prolixitate inopinato expediat.\n[[425.12]] Sunt et aliae methodi investigandi theoremata, per analogiam aliorum jam inventorum:\n[[425.13]] ita ex iis quae de circulo demonstraverat Euclides, video Apollonium de\n[[425.14]] conicis conjectasse non pauca, quae calculo postea vera invenit: praeclarus in eam\n[[425.15]] rem usus est methodi meae de figurarum harmonia. Vide quae Gregorius dixit in\n[[425.16]] libro de Circuli, Ellipsis ac Hyperbolae quadratura, quae suo quodam modo etiam ad\n[[425.17]] Rectam et Parabolam produci poterant. Et ope theorematum conicorum non difficile\n[[425.18]] erit invenire Theoremata multa pro gradibus altioribus.\n[[425.19]] Superest methodus investigandi per inductionem, sed cum omnia percurrere nequeamus,\n[[425.20]] artis est eligere prae caeteris examinanda, et hoc jam reducitur ad Analogiam;\n[[425.21]] et in eo consistit tota ars experimentorum. Quanquam fateor vel nos simpliciter\n[[425.22]] quaerere experimenta dato subjecto; vel speciatim quaerere dato phaenomeno\n[[425.23]] causam, quod peculiaris est opera; eo enim pertinent quae de instantiis crucis, aliisque\n[[425.24]] dixit Baconus. Sed simpliciter experimenta quaerere dato subjecto, hoc faciendum\n[[425.25]] est, ope jam cognitorum experimentorum per analogiam. Analogia autem in\n[[426.1]] eo fundatur, ut quae in multis conveniunt aut opposita sunt, ea in datis quoque vicinis\n[[426.2]] ad priora convenire aut opposita esse suspicemur.\n[[426.3]] Sunt Experimenta quaedam, quae potius Observationes nominantur, quae considerari\n[[426.4]] tantum, non produci opus. Talia sunt experimenta quae numeros consideranti\n[[426.5]] offerunt sese; item observationes coelestes, item de ventis, aestu; aliisque quae\n[[426.6]] discere possumus tantum interrogando. Et in his nihil utique negligere deberemus,\n[[426.7]] quando tam facile est ea addiscere; opus autem est diariis in eam rem, ac velut\n[[426.8]] Tabulis, et postea Tabularum collationibus, ad harmonias quasdam, sive analogias\n[[426.9]] constabiliendas.\n[[426.10]] Ars faciendi Hypotheses, sive Ars conjectandi diversi generis est, huc pertinet\n[[426.11]] ars explicandi Cryptographemata, quae pro maximo haberi debet specimine artis\n[[426.12]] conjectandi purae et a materia abstractae, unde regulae duci possunt quas postea\n[[426.13]] etiam materiae applicare liceat.\n",
  "number": "46.",
  "title": "Schediasma de arte inveniendi theoremata",
  "date": ""
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:46. Schediasma de arte inveniendi theoremata 421.16;0:63:046:74! :L:l^. 7. September 1674 De Arte inveniendi Theoremata. Artem problemata solvendi tantum ab Analyticis tractatam constat. Theoremata autem fassi sunt omnes, casu inveniri: nam quis mortalium praevidere possit exitum combinationum valde...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>